message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "PhenologyPro: a browser-based platform for agroclimatology and crop phenology"
abstract: >-
  PhenologyPro is a self-contained web application that carries the daily series of a weather station
  through a whole agroclimatic study in the browser, with no installation and no server-side computation.
  It describes the climate of the site (normals, Walter–Lieth climograph, frost-free period, aridity
  indices), accumulates thermal time by six degree-day methods with three upper-threshold cut-offs, computes
  reference evapotranspiration by FAO-56 Penman–Monteith with the prescribed procedures for missing data and
  by Hargreaves–Samani, Priestley–Taylor, Thornthwaite and Turc, builds the crop coefficient curve corrected
  to the local climate, runs the Thornthwaite–Mather monthly balance and the FAO-56 daily root-zone balance,
  schedules irrigation, dates the BBCH stages of a crop and calibrates their thermal requirements, counts
  winter chill by chill hours, Utah units and the Dynamic model, and estimates frost and heat risk and the
  sowing window. Every equation is cited to its source and checked against the worked examples of FAO-56.
